{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power power","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","fileName":"Power.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Exponents and Roots]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Base of a Power","Exponent","Square","Cube","Geometric Progression","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power power","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","fileName":"Power.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power","heading":"Power","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A power is an expression (a^n) formed from a [[Base of a Power]] and an [[Exponent]]. For positive integer (n), its value is the product of (n) copies of (a).\n\nThe second and third powers have special names: a [[Square]] and a [[Cube]]. Powers compress repeated structure and make patterns such as growth in a [[Geometric Progression]] easy to express. They follow the [[Laws of Exponents]], which permit products, quotients, and nested powers to be simplified without expanding every repeated factor.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Base of a Power","Exponent","Square","Cube","Geometric Progression","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"power power","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Power.md","fileName":"Power.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Power","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Exponents and Roots","Base of a Power","Exponent","Square","Cube","Geometric Progression","Laws of Exponents","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}